The next development phase will focus on extending the existing SessionRecorder so that interview records can be persisted in PostgreSQL instead of relying exclusively on local JSON files.
This transition will preserve the existing V3 interview workflow while introducing structured persistence.
Subsequent phases will implement historical interview retrieval, Diagnosis Agent integration, validated Orchestrator interactions, and clinician-facing report generation.
Important: The current implementation establishes the database infrastructure and initial schema. It does not yet mean that the running chatbot persists its interviews in PostgreSQL. That integration will be implemented and tested in the next phase.
